y=\"sans-serif\">• الْأَجْرُ ، النِّعْمَةُ (Ajr, Ne'mat) → الْأَجْرُ ، الْمَغْفِرَةُ ، التَّقْوَىٰ ، الزَّلْزَلَةُ (Badla, Bakhshish, Parhezgari, Zalzalah).</text>\n  <text x=\"26\" y=\"170\" fill=\"#94a3b8\" font-size=\"12\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">• Unit 1 mein aasaan Qur'ani alfaaz aur buniyadi ishaare/qawa'id sikhaye gaye hain.</text>\n</svg>\n</div>\n**Qaa'ida (Pages 22–23):** Is sabaq mein ajr, maghfirat, taqwa aur aakhirat se muta'alliq 36 aham Qur'ani asmaa aur 12 Qur'ani aayatein shamil hain."
